<div class="stx"><p>I think in <span class="tok" style="--c: #5B9BEA"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #3178C6"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#ts"></use></svg></b>TypeScript</span> and speak fluent <span class="tok" style="--c: #E8CB3A"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #F7DF1E"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#js"></use></svg></b>JavaScript</span>. Interfaces take shape in <span class="tok" style="--c: #61DAFB"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #61DAFB"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#react"></use></svg></b>React</span> and <span class="tok" style="--c: var(--fg)"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #EDEEF0"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#next"></use></svg></b>Next.js</span>, dressed in <span class="tok" style="--c: #38BDF8"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #06B6D4"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#tailwind"></use></svg></b>Tailwind</span>. Client state stays light with <span class="tok" style="--c: #D4A373"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #D4A373"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#zustand"></use></svg></b>Zustand</span>; server data stays fresh with <span class="tok" style="--c: #F472B6"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #FF4154"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#rq"></use></svg></b>React Query</span>. Data rests in <span class="tok" style="--c: #7FA7DB"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #7FA7DB"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#pg"></use></svg></b>PostgreSQL</span>, shaped by <span class="tok" style="--c: #C5F74F"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #C5F74F"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#drizzle"></use></svg></b>Drizzle</span> and kept close by <span class="tok" style="--c: #FF4D4D"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #FF4438"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#redis"></use></svg></b>Redis</span>, while files and images settle into <span class="tok" style="--c: #F29D38"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #F29D38"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#s3"></use></svg></b>AWS S3</span>. It all runs on <span class="tok" style="--c: #6CC24A"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #5FA04E"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#node"></use></svg></b>Node.js</span>, builds with <span class="tok" style="--c: #B07CFF"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #9135FF"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#vite"></use></svg></b>Vite</span>, and ships to the edge on <span class="tok" style="--c: var(--fg)"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #EDEEF0"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#vercel"></use></svg></b>Vercel</span> and <span class="tok" style="--c: #F38020"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #F38020"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#cf"></use></svg></b>Cloudflare</span> — and nothing ships until <span class="tok" style="--c: #FF7A66"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #F44B21"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#lh"></use></svg></b>Lighthouse</span> agrees it's fast.</p><p class="stx2">After hours, I'm picking up <span class="tok lrn" style="--c: #29BEB0"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #00ADD8"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#go"></use></svg></b>Go</span> because simple should also be fast, losing friendly arguments with <span class="tok lrn" style="--c: #DEA584"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #DEA584"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#rust"></use></svg></b>Rust</span>'s borrow checker, and smuggling near-native speed into the browser with <span class="tok lrn" style="--c: #7C8CFF"><b class="lgw" style="--h: #654FF0"><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/stack.svg#wasm"></use></svg></b>WebAssembly</span>.</p></div>
